<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Ideal sowing weather continues.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Ideal sowing weather continues.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ideal planting and harvesting weather continued over the weekend across the High Plains, grain dealers said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We had another beautiful weekend for harvesting and planting, and it looks like it could stay that way until maybe Thursday,&quot; a central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers in Oklahoma said the skies were clear but the winds had been fairly strong.</p>
<p>&quot;Planting went ahead on schedule, but we had a lot of wind. A lot of dirt was moving,&quot; said a dealer in north central Oklahoma.</p>
<p>Another dealer in northeast Oklahoma said winds of between 16 and 20 miles per hour blew Saturday and Sunday.</p>
<p>Basis bids were mixed, with some strength reported in Oklahoma and Texas.  </p>
